meta {
  name: Restart Attempt
  type: http
  seq: 31
}

patch {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/college-admin/assessments/attempts/{{assessmentAttemptId}}/restart
  body: none
  auth: none
}

headers {
  Authorization: Bearer {{staffToken}}
}

docs {
  Hard-DELETES the attempt entirely (not a reset in place) — works from
  ANY status (completed, auto_submitted, terminated, under_evaluation,
  evaluated, result_published), not just a stuck in_progress one.

  Response: `{ application_id }` — there's no attempt left to return.
  After this call, the student's application has NO attempt at all, so
  their next `POST /student/assessments/attempts { application_id }` is a
  genuinely fresh start (it's no longer blocked by the "you already have
  an attempt for this application" uniqueness check, since that row is
  gone).

  This is a deliberate exception to this codebase's "soft deletes only"
  rule — an attempt + its answers being explicitly discarded by an
  authorized admin action, not a business record with its own lifecycle.
  StudentAnswer rows cascade-delete automatically. AssessmentReschedule
  rows for this attempt (if any) are also deleted first, defensively —
  that table has no cascade and no module code writes to it yet, but this
  avoids a future FK violation once that feature exists.

  Scope note: only the attempt is deleted. The linked ApplicationCourse's
  pipeline status (e.g. "assessment_completed" if it was already
  evaluated/published) is deliberately left untouched — restarting does
  NOT revert it back to an earlier stage.

  404 if the attempt doesn't exist or belongs to a different college.
}
